The broad comparison starts with all **22,406 shared exact gene labels**, not a regulator panel. Primary eligibility yields 6,089 genes including Pmp22. Matching uses only the two untreated abundances; Pmp22 is excluded from references. Wider/narrower abundance windows and nearest-neighbor sets preserve the main departure. The late 8-hour MEF versus 7-hour NIH3T3 comparison is secondary: its target difference is +2.857 log2, but it is not time-matched. Table S5B's 8-hour label conflicts with GEO and Methods and remains explicit.

The program comparison localizes the effect. Relative to those 42 late-cluster genes, Pmp22 MEF induction is at the 19th percentile at 2 h and 43rd at 8 h, whereas its NIH3T3 response is at the 7th percentile at both sampled times. Three reference genes have still lower NIH3T3 responses. Thus this is chiefly poor transfer of the MEF induction pattern into NIH3T3, not uniquely strong MEF induction. Authoritative ranks use explicit floor handling in `late-cluster-axis-ranks.tsv`; an earlier interactive calculation with undefined zero ratios was not retained as evidence.

There is **one deposited library per condition**. Genes are reference measurements, not independent biological replicates. Percentiles and reference quantiles are descriptive; no gene bootstrap, population p-value or biological confidence interval is claimed. MEFs received 1 µM thapsigargin and NIH3T3 cells 200 nM, with different culture supplements. Dose, cell model, culture history and potential line/background effects remain inseparable. No matched total RNA or absolute synthesis calibration exists in these footprint tables. A rise in relative footprints can coexist with reduced absolute synthesis during global stress repression. Mapping artifacts and sample-specific effects remain possible.

The new RNA-decay branch is source-tested but already known. [Hollien et al. (2009)](https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC2728407/), Table I, reports Pmp22 RNA log2 stress/control −0.88 after human IRE1 reconstitution versus −0.07 in IRE1-deficient MEFs: approximately 0.543 versus 0.953-fold, interaction −0.81 log2. The source averages three independently repeated experiments, using 2 mM DTT for 6 h. Its table records decreased Pmp22 stability. Our script extracts all 26 selected rows, preserving seven stability-positive, four stability-negative and fifteen untested entries; it does not fabricate a whole-transcriptome universe or replicate uncertainty. Main Figures 1 and 3 test other targets, so their nuclease-mutant results must not be described as a direct PMP22 experiment. The linked S2 timecourse was not recovered; legitimate routes and failures are recorded.

[Moore and Hollien (2015)](https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC4571326/) further shows substrate-dependent coupling of PERK-mediated translation attenuation to IRE1 decay, using other RNA targets and reporters. That provides a mechanistic alternative, not proof of the same coupling for PMP22. A reduced exact-symbol RIDD panel in our footprint data has only two eligible non-Pmp22 comparators, Hgsnat and Galnt10; both decline in both contexts. Other source aliases or low-abundance targets remain excluded explicitly. This small exploratory panel does not establish a RIDD signature or identify the cause of the discrepancy.

Novelty is separate from support. [Gonen et al. (2019)](https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC6416471/) already published the source values, late-cluster membership and broad program transfer between these cell types. [Guan et al. (2017)](https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC5730339/) explicitly discussed PMP22's chronic stress regulation. RIDD and general context dependence are also prior results. What is new here is the **executed baseline-matched quantification, its count-based robustness, and the qualification that published program membership partly accounts for it**. The exact matched-reference inference was not found in the inspected source papers and targeted searches; this is a scoped analytical contribution, not a global priority claim or novel biological mechanism. `novelty-audit.json` preserves queries, passages, boundaries and excluded synonym collisions with yeast GAS3.

The decisive overturning test is a replicated cell-model × dose experiment at a common time, using matched total/nascent RNA, calibrated footprints and protein synthesis, with IRE1 RNase and PERK perturbation/rescue. If Pmp22's difference falls within the preregistered baseline-matched reference distribution across independent cultures, the apparent selective departure fails to reproduce. If RNA loss fully accounts for footprint loss, a translation-specific explanation fails; if IRE1 perturbation restores RNA stability and footprints without restoring translation efficiency, decay becomes the stronger route. Human Schwann-cell transfer must then be tested separately.

